hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"949","983 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym and Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, they said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, from Adi ibn Hatim - Ibn Yahya said: and this is the hadith of Abu Nuaym - who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mirad? He said: What strikes with its edge, eat; and what strikes with its side is waqidh. He said: And I asked him about hunting with dogs. He said: What it holds for you, eat, for the taking of the dog is its slaughter. If you find with your dog another dog or other dogs, and fear it may have taken it with it and killed it, do not eat, for you mentioned the name of Allah over your dog and did not mention it over the other."
"950","984 - Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, he said: Ubayda ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Bayan Abu Bishr narrated to me, from Amir al-Shabi, who said: Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, we send trained dogs and they kill. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When they kill, eat, unless it eats from it, or another dog joins it."
"951","985 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Rabia ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: Abu Thalaba al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of People of the Book and eat in their vessels, and we are in a land of hunting, so I shoot with my bow, and hunt with my trained dog and my untrained dog. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you are in a land of People of the Book as you mentioned, do not eat in their vessels, unless you find no alternative; if you find no alternative, wash them then eat in them. And if you are in a land of hunting as you mentioned, what you hunt with your bow, mention the name of Allah and eat; what you hunt with your trained dog, mention the name of Allah and eat; and what you hunt with your untrained dog, if you reach its slaughter in time, eat."
"952","986 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh informed me, that he heard Rabia ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi say: I heard Abu Idris al-Khawlani say: He heard Abu Thalaba al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned the story of the dog alone. And he said at its end: And whatever you do not reach in time for its slaughter, do not eat, in the story of the untrained dog."
"953","987 - Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratisi narrated to us, he said: Ubayda ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Bayan, from al-Shabi, who said: Adi ibn Hatim said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the mirad. He said: If it pierces, eat; if it strikes with its side, do not eat."
"954","988 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Said - narrated to us, from Shuba, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, who said: Adi ibn Hatim said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and seek its trail after a night, and find my arrow in it. He said: If you find it with your arrow in it and no beast has eaten from it, eat."
"955","989 - He said: I mentioned it to Abu Bishr, and he said, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you find your arrow in it and see no trace in it from other than it, knowing that it killed it, eat."
"956","990 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Abi Zaida - narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If your shot falls into water and it drowns, do not eat."
"957","991 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and seek the trail after a night. He said: If you find your arrow in it and no beast has eaten from it, eat."
"958","992 - Shuba said: I mentioned it to Abu Bishr and he narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you find your arrow in it and see no trace in it from other than it, knowing that it killed it, eat."
